WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Two cftc exchanges sued Missouri to stop the state treating sports contracts as bets. This is prediction-market's daily, episode 27. Journalism and education, never a bet. North American derivatives exchange, the cftc registered shop behind Crypto.com's platform, and Novig's Ludlow Exchange filed those complaints on October 16. They want federal judges to stop Missouri from applying its sports wagering statute to the sports event contracts. Attorney General Catherine Hanaway had already

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:36.220
written both firms, plus Kalshi, Polymarket, Robinhood, and Underdog on September 16th and

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:36.940
17th.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.060
Her office announced the letters on September 18th.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.540
Each company got 30 days to pull the contracts or take a gaming commission license.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.460
A license means a 10% tax on adjusted gross sports wagering revenue, and fees that can

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.840
hit $500,000 at the start and again every 5 years.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.040
Ludlow became a designated contract market on June 16th.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:04.880
It's complaint calls the contract swaps and says the Commodity Exchange Act gives the CFTC exclusive jurisdiction.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:13.280
Novig wants a preliminary injunction, so nothing changes while the 8th Circuit briefs Kalshi's Iowa appeal, Kalshi EX versus Bird.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.600
Crypto.com's complaint was still off the public docket as of Sunday.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.540
Reporting on it says the company wants a declaratory judgment and a permanent injunction.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:27.680
That filing says the letter went to Forrest Dax, not the exchange, and that a Missouri

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.500
license is not a real option because the state constitution allows only two direct mobile

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.920
sports wagering licenses, and both are already awarded.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:41.580
Kalshi, Polymarket, Robinhood, and Underdog had not sued in either Missouri Federal District

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.440
as of Sunday.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.180
Hannah Ways Office has described ongoing talks with Kalshi.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.500
Her letters call the products unlicensed sports wagering.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.640
They say most federal courts to hear the question have found the Commodity Exchange Act does

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.720
not preempt state gambling law and that these contracts are not swaps.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.680
She put it this way, companies cannot evade Missouri law by dressing sports betting

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.020
up as event contracts.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:12.300
Her office also said Crypto.com lets users in at 18 under Missouri's floor of 21, a complaint

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.420
she raised with five of the six firms and not with Novig.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.369
Tariq Mansour used a Washington stage this week to draw the industry's line.

00:02:20.829 --> 00:02:28.029
At DC FinTech Week, 2026, the lines.com reports, he said Kalshi feels pretty good about the court fights.

00:02:28.429 --> 00:02:33.429
He then called the stakes a choice of whether prediction markets exist in the United States or go offshore,

00:02:34.049 --> 00:02:39.769
and said federal jurisdiction under the Commodity Exchange Act is better than a fragmented patchwork of state laws.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:43.929
Sports without economic consequence, he said, is a ludicrous notion.

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:49.864
Carly Johnson, research director at the American Gaming Association, described a different

00:02:49.864 --> 00:02:51.864
fight on Monday in the Las Vegas sun.

00:02:52.424 --> 00:02:57.024
The association's study, playing the numbers, found gamblers, outscored non-gamblers

00:02:57.024 --> 00:03:01.504
on financial literacy, and sportsbetters came out on top in every group measured.

00:03:02.104 --> 00:03:06.764
Prediction market users, she said, have the confidence of sportsbetters and the math skills

00:03:06.764 --> 00:03:08.504
of someone who does not bet at all.

00:03:08.984 --> 00:03:14.024
Those users, in her account, sit on platforms offering sports contracts without the responsible

00:03:14.024 --> 00:03:18.784
gaming tools, state license sportsbooks must provide, while the products are marketed

00:03:18.784 --> 00:03:19.604
as investing.

00:03:20.144 --> 00:03:25.444
The association filed an amicus brief in October, backing New Jersey's petition for the US Supreme

00:03:25.444 --> 00:03:29.764
Court to decide whether states can regulate markets such as Kalshi and Polymarket.

00:03:30.264 --> 00:03:36.424
The NFL filed its own brief, so did a coalition of 39 states in Washington, D.C., which said

00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:38.704
the split has resulted in chaos nationwide.

00:03:39.484 --> 00:03:41.584
Johnson's spending comparison is concrete.

00:03:41.584 --> 00:03:48.264
Regulated gaming puts about $472 million a year into responsible gaming programs, and

00:03:48.264 --> 00:03:53.824
gaming taxes supply over 130 million a year for problem gambling services, where she

00:03:53.824 --> 00:03:55.664
said, prediction markets pay zero.

00:03:56.676 --> 00:04:00.376
Polymarket has a new contract on whether France declares a state of siege.

00:04:00.916 --> 00:04:07.196
The listing price is a declaration by October 31st or November 15th at roughly 1-3%, and

00:04:07.196 --> 00:04:09.456
a year-end price around 15%.

00:04:09.456 --> 00:04:15.336
Article 36 of the French Constitution, the listing says, requires imminent peril from foreign

00:04:15.336 --> 00:04:18.076
war or armed insurrection before a state of siege.

00:04:18.676 --> 00:04:24.256
President Emmanuel Macron and Interior Minister Laurent Nunez have ruled out a state of emergency.

00:04:25.219 --> 00:04:32.199
On the board today, the 2028 Republican presidential nomination prices JD Vance at 44% on polymarket,

00:04:32.779 --> 00:04:34.499
down three and a half points in a day.

00:04:34.499 --> 00:04:42.299
Brazil's presidential election price is Flavio Bolsonaro at 77.2% on polymarket, down 3.6

00:04:42.299 --> 00:04:42.839
points.

00:04:43.339 --> 00:04:50.699
Israel's next prime minister prices Gadi Eisenkot at 47.9% on polymarket, down 5.2 points.

00:04:51.179 --> 00:04:55.459
The US House prices the Democratic Party at 90.1% on Kalshi.

00:04:56.099 --> 00:05:01.199
A manifold question on whether another millennium prize problem gets solved in 2026 prices

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:02.979
yes at 34%.

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:06.239
That venue is play money, mana, not dollars.

00:05:06.879 --> 00:05:10.559
Access to CalShi, polymarket, and the rest depends on where you live.

00:05:11.119 --> 00:05:14.879
The rules differ by country, province, and state, and they are changing.

00:05:15.619 --> 00:05:19.899
CalShi's question on who becomes President Trump's next press secretary is a new listing

00:05:19.899 --> 00:05:21.039
from the last three days.

00:05:21.679 --> 00:05:24.779
Scott Jennings and Anna Kelly are each at 15%.

00:05:24.779 --> 00:05:30.079
Kelly up four points from the previous day's price, and Elizabeth Pipco is at 5%.

00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:35.668
A 95 cent contract is not free money, and how it works starts with the payout.

00:05:35.928 --> 00:05:40.768
The Globe and Mail describes these contracts as paying $1 if the stated outcome hits,

00:05:41.188 --> 00:05:45.768
and nothing if it does not, at a price somewhere between 1 cent and 99 cents.

00:05:46.228 --> 00:05:49.088
You lock that price and any fee until resolution.

00:05:49.608 --> 00:05:55.408
5 cents is the whole possible gain on a 95 cent contract, and a miss takes the 95 cents.

00:05:55.848 --> 00:05:57.488
Those 5 cents are not interest.

00:05:57.488 --> 00:06:02.588
Canadian dealers reach the same US listings on a different fee card. The Canadian

00:06:02.588 --> 00:06:07.948
investment regulatory organization lets authorized investment dealers offer a limited set of event

00:06:07.948 --> 00:06:13.568
contracts cleared through certain CFTC regulated exchanges. Right now, that permission covers

00:06:13.568 --> 00:06:19.028
wealth simple and interactive brokers Canada only. Wealth simple predict offers a subset

00:06:19.028 --> 00:06:24.648
of CalShi contracts and charges two US cents per contract upfront. A contract priced at

00:06:24.648 --> 00:06:31.628
42 U.S. cents, therefore costs 44. A correct call pays $1. A wrong call loses the $0.44.

00:06:32.488 --> 00:06:37.708
Interactive brokers Canada charges 2 U.S. cents a contract on Calche, and 1 U.S.

00:06:37.808 --> 00:06:43.528
cent on Forecast X. Direct Calche fees by contrast move with the price and with how many contracts

00:06:43.528 --> 00:06:50.328
you buy. 100 contracts at 1 U.S. cent each would cost 63 U.S. cents in fees on Calche itself.

00:06:50.328 --> 00:06:55.808
The same 100 through wealth-simple predict would cost two US dollars in fees, more than

00:06:55.808 --> 00:06:56.928
three times as much.

00:06:57.448 --> 00:06:59.348
At 50 US cents, the gap shrinks.

00:06:59.888 --> 00:07:06.208
100 contracts would cost $1.75 in Kalshi fees against $2 on wealth-simple predict.

00:07:06.648 --> 00:07:11.328
Two cents is 20% of a 10-cent contract and 4% of a 50-cent contract.

00:07:11.968 --> 00:07:17.448
Benjamin Felix, chief investment officer at PWL Capital, told the Globe that on a cheap

00:07:17.448 --> 00:07:20.408
contract, those percentage fees get significant fast.

00:07:20.828 --> 00:07:24.068
The contract's trade in US dollars, so currency is another toll.

00:07:24.748 --> 00:07:30.108
Wealth's simple standard conversion fee is 1.5% on a live rate that includes a spread

00:07:30.518 --> 00:07:33.788
unless the client already holds US dollars and moves them over.

00:07:34.368 --> 00:07:40.468
Interactive Broker's Canada starts conversion at 2000s of 1%, with no added spread, but

00:07:40.468 --> 00:07:44.568
a $2 minimum means a small conversion cost more than that rate suggests.

00:07:45.288 --> 00:07:50.308
Felix's line is that a per-contract fee plus a currency fee adds up quickly and aggressively,

00:07:50.808 --> 00:07:54.268
and that net of those costs the arithmetic stacks against the trader.

00:07:54.868 --> 00:08:00.008
Subtract the fee before you read the gap to $1 as a return, and subtract a conversion if

00:08:00.008 --> 00:08:01.928
your dollars are not the contracts dollars.

00:08:02.568 --> 00:08:07.288
On the globe's one-cent example, the trading fee alone can exceed the price of the contracts.

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:11.728
A price near a dollar leaves an even thinner remainder for a flat fee to eat.

00:08:11.728 --> 00:08:14.568
The number on the screen is the cost of a claim.

